{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1384541-some-questions-on-db-charms-and-character-building","id":1384541,"title":"Some questions on DB charms and character building","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-28T18:40:47-07:00","id":1384541,"title":"Some questions on DB charms and character building","content":"Hey gang, <br /> At long last I found an Exalted game! And a DB game, my favorite splat that doesn't rhyme with &quot;Midereal&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I've been lurking around the forums, there is a ton of great advice, and I have some questions I'm hoping people have insight on.<br /> <br /> The Aura system is interesting. I think for combat charms my plan is to stick in aspect (that gives me an excuse to do IMA) so Aura doesn't trip me up, at least for my first character. But I'm wondering if people find Aura is as much of a consideration when it comes to the social side of charms? I know that's an really broad question. For instance, my vague plan is to head maybe five or more charms into socialize, at the very least get up to Auspicious First Meeting Attitude. I'm not seeing too many charms in socialize with aura effects, and so it doesn't seem like there is a big difference between a fire aspect using those charms versus water or air. Am I correct? If so, is this notably less true in other trees?<br /> <br /> Also, for combat capability my plan was to at least take the IMA up to the form charm. If I'm a Fire aspect, should I grab some dodge charms as well? If I'm Air, should I supplement the style with thrown and/or stealth charms (or maybe heavenly typhoon evocations)? Speaking of Air, I was also looking at water dragon and eventually (prob after chargen?) some ebon shadow. Would both that and Air end up making a more ninja-like character? What would the differences be?<br /> <br /> Lastly, I kinda love that the righteous devil form charm makes it work with wood dragon. It gives me the image of a (to put it mildly) unorthodox dancing immaculate cowboy monk. Do those styles actually support each other well?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4620-tumbleweed664","name":"tumbleweed664","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T21:08:14-07:00","id":1384560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tumbleweed664</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1384541-some-questions-on-db-charms-and-character-building#post1384541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Aura system is interesting. I think for combat charms my plan is to stick in aspect (that gives me an excuse to do IMA) so Aura doesn't trip me up, at least for my first character. But I'm wondering if people find Aura is as much of a consideration when it comes to the social side of charms? I know that's an really broad question. For instance, my vague plan is to head maybe five or more charms into socialize, at the very least get up to Auspicious First Meeting Attitude. I'm not seeing too many charms in socialize with aura effects, and so it doesn't seem like there is a big difference between a fire aspect using those charms versus water or air. Am I correct? If so, is this notably less true in other trees?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most DB social trees interact less with Aura than the combat trees, and also just by the nature of it and the fact that the excellency is Mute and stuff flaring totemic and locking yourself out of another aura isn't as much of a concern. That being said, there's some pretty awesome uses of Aura in those trees that you might want to consider. Even without being Aura locked it's still easier to get into your own aspect's Aura by doing something like stunting a threat with a crackling of electricity around your fingers or some-such.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tumbleweed664</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1384541-some-questions-on-db-charms-and-character-building#post1384541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, for combat capability my plan was to at least take the IMA up to the form charm. If I'm a Fire aspect, should I grab some dodge charms as well? If I'm Air, should I supplement the style with thrown and/or stealth charms (or maybe heavenly typhoon evocations)? Speaking of Air, I was also looking at water dragon and eventually (prob after chargen?) some ebon shadow. Would both that and Air end up making a more ninja-like character? What would the differences be?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Air Dragon</b><br /> <br /> Air Dragon is one of the most alter-ability dependent styles in the game, but that's not necessarily a bad thing. With it you really want to grab Dodge, Athletics and Stealth as abilities, and maybe a few charms in them. If you have Heirs to the Shogunate there's some particularly solid new Air based Dodge, Athletics and Stealth charms in there. If you're getting Heavenly Typhoon I'd also invest in Occult. Thrown charms are not necessary but if you've got the ability dots and charms to spare some of them can be fun, but you can't use them in conjunction with your MA.<br /> <br /> The main strategies of the style involve Thrown's strengths, namely getting into Close range with archers, and staying at Short range against everyone else, being exactly where they don't want you. It's also exceptional anywhere you can take advantage of terrain elevation or difficult terrain, and of course stealth attacks. It's a lot of investment, but for that you'll get a good combat style, the ability to run up smoke, vanish into thin air, and annihilate spirits, as well as having both a good doge and parry score in the event of unblockable/undodgeable attacks.<br /> <br /> You might think about gettting Midnight Thorn with this one, it's a jade chain shirt from Arms.<br /> <br /> <b>Earth Dragon</b><br /> <br /> Not much to say with this except it's really solid and also really straight forward. Just hit things, often with smashing attacks, and soak damage. Heavy armor is the best choice for combat, but the mobility penalty can sometimes suck, so going unarmored with resistance charms isn't the worst thing in the world. Also a style that taking three dex and maxing out strength and stamina might not be the worst idea, depending on your campaign. Maybe grab Faith's Pillar or Fist of Titans. Mela's Coil is also a good armor. In fact it's probably the best armor in the game.<br /> <br /> <b>Fire Dragon</b><br /> <br /> Doesn't actually blend that well with dodge, most of its charms specify you need to parry with them. Definitely pair it with a strong Awareness though, and if you're into mixing styles it goes pretty amazing with Steel Devil, depending on your campaign. It doesn't work very well against enemies that have really high defense, and penalty ignoring charms, and high soak, for example. You might want to pair with Smiling Razors, if you do though get Stealth as well as Larceny its evocations are based around smokey sneak attacks and infiltration. Likewise Midnight Thorn.<br /> <br /> I'd also watch out with it. Like a lot of Fire charms in general, the trick with Fire Dragon is actually knowing when to burn out, and when to simmer. With it's Join Battle boosting charm and it's other charms that add bonuses to decisive attacks and reflexive activations for going first, a possible strategy is to just blow 30+ motes in the very first turn of combat and just <i>end </i>something, but then that's it, your mote pool is cold ash after that.<br /> <br /> <b>Water Dragon</b><br /> <br /> Not much to say on this either, it's just solid and pretty straightforward. The only thing is it deals in a lot of wound penalty stuff, so the best strategy with it is probably not to wait until you have 40 initiative and destroy something, but more to give them death by degrees as they drown. It combos well with ally attacks that give enhanced wound penalties. It can pair well with Tiger Style if you want to be aggressive, or Ebon Shadow if you want to be a ninja.<br /> <br /> Vengeant, the razor claws, are cool, but very...angry. For an angry Iselsi murderer though that's a good thing.<br /> <br /> <b>Wood Dragon</b><br /> <br /> Kind of a super weird style. If you're going to be really social with this one grabbing the Red Jade Powerbow Heartsong might be a good fit, also getting it with archery. It doesn't pair especially well with Righteous Devil, but like Archery it will let you attack at range and fight at close range if you want to. It also just pairs well with Performance anyway as some of the attacks use it. Also if you get this style pump your Stamina and get ox-bodies, and maybe some healing magic as well. It's a really rugged style for that reason.<br /> <br /> It also pairs well with White Reaper style, which can also use staves. Archery/RD style complement it by giving you variety, WR style just adds more effects onto what you were already doing.<br /> <br /> If you're looking for artifacts the Daring Venture V'Neef family one is pretty good. You can't use a full longbow while mounted so Hundred Rivers is just a combat companion or non-combat mount if you wanted to use Archery, otherwise you can just ride him around using the bow as a staff and dismounting to shoot if you ever need to. Get survival with it though.<br /> <br /> The other ones you might use are Calumny, the Green Jade Wrackstaff of house Cynis, which is awesome to use for a social character because it steals secrets from people. Or you can use Sekhem, the Red Jade Dragon Sigh Wand, it doesn't give much synergy but it is cool and its bayonet counts as an artifact as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tumbleweed664</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1384541-some-questions-on-db-charms-and-character-building#post1384541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lastly, I kinda love that the righteous devil form charm makes it work with wood dragon. It gives me the image of a (to put it mildly) unorthodox dancing immaculate cowboy monk. Do those styles actually support each other well?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, you'll almost never use their charms together to make something even more powerful, but it does let you have two completely unique fighting styles without having to attune to different weapons and stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T00:09:32-07:00","id":1384587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tumbleweed664</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1384541-some-questions-on-db-charms-and-character-building#post1384541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But I'm wondering if people find Aura is as much of a consideration when it comes to the social side of charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it's very manageable.<br /> <br /> NPCs have Resolve scores of 1-5. You can't convince anyone without an Intimacy, so you're looking at 0-8 before Charms, Willpower and Stunts. 0-17 worst case. But the fact is, most NPCs have 2-3 Resolve, eating a -1 from an Intimacy, and you're throwing at least a 2-die stunt. Even as a Dragon-Blooded, you have to pretty much trip over and swallow your tongue to fail social rolls (unless you're trying something crazy like convincing Ahlat to destroy Harborhead -- I mapped out how to do that with a Solar in another thread).<br /> <br /> As you basically don't need Charms at all, Aura isn't pivotal. Charms are gravy.<br /> <br /> Exalted gives you stats for the typical farmer or shop keeper. Resolve 1, Guile 1. It gives you stats for an exotic and successful caravan merchant - 4. It gives you stats for one of the most powerful gods in Creation 5/4.<br /> <br /> Take Ahlat. Resolve 5. Have an adversial ST who says Ahlat views all Dragon-Blooded as cowards and traitors. Resolve 9.<br /> <br /> Let's say you want him to bless your army so Harbourhead isn't wiped out by Alchemicals. Resolve 7. You make a speach, referencing your love of the city asking the god to set aside your differences and win glory on the battlefield in defense of all Creation; +1 Success and +2 dice. You spend Willpower; +1 Success. 4m Excellency adds exploding 10s and two more Successes. You now only need to roll 3 successes, which should be easily doable on Charisma 3 Presence 4 plus two from the Stunt (84% certainty before the exploding 10s).<br /> <br /> Yes, Ahlat could Stunt/Willpower that up to 5-7 successes needed. But equally you could use the Air Anima power, have Charisma/Presence 5, Specailty, and tag the &quot;War is the Crucible of Heroes&quot; Intimacy. (If both sides go All In then, keeping the PC at a Level 2 Stunt, it's Resolve 12, dropped to 9 with 5 automatic successes, so trying for 4 successes on 17 dice with exploding 10s... 97% certainty of success.)<br /> <br /> So long as you're trying to do reasonable things, you won't really need Charms like Hot Blooded Ardor -- let alone the awesome Aura effects of Hot Blooded Ardor.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not seeing too many charms in socialize with aura effects, and so it doesn't seem like there is a big difference between a fire aspect using those charms versus water or air. Am I correct? If so, is this notably less true in other trees? </div> </div> </div>Some trees have very good Aura effects. But, again, Social Influence is predictable. Read/Instill/Persuade. It's easy enough to set up Aura.<br /> <br /> Usually you are not going to flair your Anima during a Social scene (at least not all the way to Bonfire), so it's really easy to just set up whichever Aura you need regardless of Aspect -- Aura just limits your combos.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I'm a Fire aspect, should I grab some dodge charms as well? </div> </div> </div>Yes. Dodge is essential.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a> is absolutely correct that Evasion is useless to you. Disengage (and Heat of Battle Advance) are <i>essential</i> to you. Buy Dodge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I'm Air, should I supplement the style with thrown and/or stealth charms (or maybe heavenly typhoon evocations)? Speaking of Air, I was also looking at water dragon and eventually (prob after chargen?) some ebon shadow. Would both that and Air end up making a more ninja-like character? What would the differences be? </div> </div> </div>Thrown is a waste. It's nice to have if you have spare dots, but you won't have spare dots.<br /> Stealth is great.<br /> Heavenly Typhoon is great (so are Occult Charms).<br /> <br /> Water Dragon will mess with your Aura and Form weapons. Fortunately, Air is more of a ultilty style than a combat style. But Air Anima is going to lock you out of Water Aura.<br /> <br /> Ebon Shadow combos nicely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lastly, I kinda love that the righteous devil form charm makes it work with wood dragon. It gives me the image of a (to put it mildly) unorthodox dancing immaculate cowboy monk. Do those styles actually support each other well? </div> </div> </div>I looked at this myself and Asked the Devs which Charms combo.<br /> <br /> Long story short, it's expensive for what it does. But a cowboy who burns his enemies as he regenerates is a pretty sweet character idea.<br /> <br /> (Do note that Wood Dragon uses a Staff, not a Spear, so no bayonets.)<br /> <br /> If you want to play it, do it.<br /> If you want to optimize, don't do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-30-2020, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T19:41:48-07:00","id":1384762,"title":"","content":"<br /> Thank you, Dr Love Monkey and John Doe! This is very helpful. I plan to grab Heirs when it drops, with any luck someone in the group was a backer and has the preview pdf.<br /> <br /> How do DBs fair with the social martial arts? Are there any not nerfed too badly by their Terrestial keywords? Or any that particularly shine when neither Terrestial nor Mastery keywords are applied (i.e. when used by a DB with an IMA)?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4620-tumbleweed664","name":"tumbleweed664","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T20:21:52-07:00","id":1384767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tumbleweed664</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1384541-some-questions-on-db-charms-and-character-building?p=1384762#post1384762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do DBs fair with the social martial arts? Are there any not nerfed too badly by their Terrestial keywords? Or any that particularly shine when neither Terrestial nor Mastery keywords are applied (i.e. when used by a DB with an IMA)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't seen them all in action with a DB, but from what I've seen of them and their terrestrial keywords I'd say that they all work pretty well. I have seen a terrestrial Dreaming Pearl stylist and they did pretty well.<br /> <br /> If you want one that pairs well with Wood Dragon probably go Dreaming Pearl, they both use Performance, although I don't think you can combo the Wood Dragon charms with the vocal weapon.<br /> <br /> I'd also look more into what kind of style of social MA you want to go with. Black Claw is a twisted manipulative style who's capstone charm involves you tearing the physical heart out of your sifu, where as the capstone for Crane style involves you gently knocking somebody out, and wiping away their bad feelings while instilling a love for all of Creation. Those are two concepts <i>pretty </i>at odds with eachother, and I wouldn't recommend taking one on a character that doesn't fit the type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T00:09:56-07:00","id":1384793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tumbleweed664</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1384541-some-questions-on-db-charms-and-character-building?p=1384762#post1384762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Thank you, Dr Love Monkey and John Doe! This is very helpful. I plan to grab Heirs when it drops, with any luck someone in the group was a backer and has the preview pdf.<br /> <br /> How do DBs fair with the social martial arts? Are there any not nerfed too badly by their Terrestial keywords? Or any that particularly shine when neither Terrestial nor Mastery keywords are applied (i.e. when used by a DB with an IMA)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I really need to make a thread about this...<br /> <br /> Exalted has two &quot;modes&quot;. The Default mode sees you create characters like the example in the Corebook and the pregens in Tomb of Dreams. The Optimized mode sees you make your characters as powerful as possible.<br /> <br /> Default, I see no reason why the social MAs shouldn't be fine. <br /> <br /> Crane Style: The big hit is Fluttering Cry of Warning. If you have a way to reliably Defend Other with your Marital Arts Parry then this'll work on am Optimized DB.<br /> <br /> Silver Voiced Nightingale Style: Voice of the Nightbird's Mastery effect is huge. Losing that sucks. Reasonable synergy with Crane.<br /> <br /> Righteous Devil Style: Reasonable synergy with Wood Dragon and White Reaper. <br /> <br /> Black Claw Style: This really suffers for a DB PC. Lots of effects capped by Essence. Multitarget dropped to single target. No Solar Performance Charms to help. It's fine if you're playing Default. OK for a Water Dragon Immaculate.<br /> <br /> Dreaming Pearl Courtesan: 2/3rds of these Charms have either (or both of) the Terrestrial or Mastery keywords. But... you can start with the Form Charm as a DB. Which means free Artifact weapon and armor. Great for Water Aspects with Water Dragon Style. Reasonable synergy with Air Dragon Style. This is the style you want to have Immaculate Martial Arts with.<br /> <br /> White Veil Style: If it existed, it would be the defining social MA. It would be disappointingly far better for Solars. Its Charms would be steeply priced for the size of Dragon-Blooded mote pools. A dedicated DB martial artist would find this combos well with the other social MAs but essentially no other style, except maybe Ebon Shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T02:42:30-07:00","id":1384815,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/\" target=\"_blank\">@JohnDoe244</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a> will give you better advice than I can, but just wanted to mention that you don\u2019t necessarily have to rely on MA to leverage your social stats in combat with DBs if you don\u2019t want to, it\u2019s something they\u2019ve historically done well with native charms.<br /> <br /> Wary Yellow Dog Attitude lets you use Socialise for JB, Fearsome Dragon Presence gives your opponent a -2 penalty for a tick, Performance has things like Vibrating Strings Defence and Petal-Strewn Pavane, the Integrity Excellency lets you ignore wound penalties, and so on.<br /> <br /> Once you hit Essence 3 and beyond and have access to things like Signature Charms, Aura of Invulnerability and Three-String Sword Prana, your \u2018capability ceiling\u2019 is maybe (to my eyes at least) higher than for a lot of the social MAs for DBs, and you\u2019re less restricted in terms of armour and weapon combos with your primary MA/combat ability.<br /> <br /> That said, social MA styles are fun and characterful as hell (John's breakdown of them above is great), so you\u2019ll hopefully have a blast if you go down that route. I personally really wanna play a DB Stealth/Larceny/White Veil master at some point.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T06:53:12-07:00","id":1384834,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24647_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24647\" data-vbnamecard=\"24647\">Moss Reynholm</a> gives good advice here.<br /> <br /> For reference, I have a mathematical background and have played Exalted since its release. But I wouldn't claim to be an expert in 3E mechanics -- I'm not a writer or a playtester or a dev. I've played (am playing) only a single game. I've done a lot of theory crafting and test matches and simple scenarios and statistical analysis. I've got decades of campaign time wracked up under the old rules.<br /> <br /> But my lack of actual play means I don't have experience with a lot of builds. Stuff like DB native charms being good is an eye opener.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T11:35:51-07:00","id":1384878,"title":"","content":"Yeah if you're not married to the idea of a martial artist, using DB native charms in combination with their more martial social charms can totally work. You probably don't want to just go pure social charms because there's not a lot of good ways to do withering attacks with them, but it's not like social MAs aren't that either. So if you want to use, say, melee, and flurry sword hits with social actions, and then finish your enemies off with a Terrifying Fire-Dragon Roar, which is a huge unblockable flamethrower breath attack out to Medium range that not only deals damage but also counts as a roll to threaten them into fleeing/rout battlegroups.<br /> <br /> Presence also has a charm in Heirs that lets you punch people's bad opinions of you away. Like, literally, it gives you bonus dice on the attack and if you deal more damage than their resolve or if you incap them you erode a negative tie towards you or instill a positive one without a roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T12:14:19-07:00","id":1384889,"title":"","content":"Thanks all, this is really helpful. Not just in the specific advice but in the way it's helping me conceptualize 3e and the charms. I'm leaning now towards a Fire aspect since it's true, socialize and presence charms bend into combat in fun ways, and I do appreciate how those charms inform the character's attitude to a degree (same with fire dragon style). I do still feel attached to MA, but maybe in conjunction with Wary Yellow Dog and some sig charm fire breath <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.That presence charm from Heirs sounds fun, I'm going to push for our DM to possibly let us swap in stuff from Heirs once it's available.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4620-tumbleweed664","name":"tumbleweed664","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T23:50:03-07:00","id":1386287,"title":"","content":"Thank you all again for your advice! I ended up making a Wood Aspect, he definitely isn't exactly where I expected to end up. I really liked Hundred Rivers but felt eh about Daring Venture aside from the wolf, so I figured I'd do the familiar part minus that bow - I'm not sure what powerbow will replace it (maybe one with better evocations than the db archery charms?).<br /> <br /> What do you all think? Are there any big holes? Points were tight, oh so tight. Integrity, socialize, and lore are getting pumped ASAP, and strength. And charisma (he's aloof, dangit!). He should probably have well bred, grandson of the Empress...<br /> <br /> How does Hundred Rivers work as a trusty mount and 3 point familiar? He is the most developed magic mount in the books that I have seen and he's undeniably flavorful for a wood aspect. But I can't tell how useful he actually is in combat. Sad that I can't actually shoot my magic bow from on top of him but I pretty much only dipped Archery and can keep a spare mundane short bow.<br /> <br /> What signatures would be good for this guy?<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>V'neef Avirat, Wood-aspect</u><br /> <br /> <u>Attributes</u><br /> Strength oo<br /> Dexterity ooooo<br /> Stamina oooo(o)<br /> <br /> Intelligence oo<br /> Wits ooo<br /> Perception oooo<br /> <br /> Charisma oo<br /> Manipulation o<br /> Appearance oooo<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Abilities</u><br /> *Archery ooo<br /> Awareness ooo<br /> *Athletics ooo<br /> *Brawl o<br /> *Dodge ooo<br /> *Integrity o (specialty?)<br /> Linguistics o<br /> Lore o<br /> *Martial arts (Wood Dragon Style) ooo(oo) (Staves)<br /> *Medicine<br /> *Performance oo(ooo) (specialty)<br /> Resistance ooo<br /> *Ride ooo(oo) (Hundred Rivers)<br /> *Survival ooo(oo)<br /> *Socialize o (Sensing Lies)<br /> <br /> <u>Merits</u><br /> Martial Arts (Wood Dragon Style) oooo<br /> Artifact (Daring Venture) ooo<br /> Mentor (Uncle Sifu) oo<br /> Familiar (bird for scouting/message delivery) o<br /> Artifact (Midnight Thorn) ooo<br /> Bonus Points: Influence (House V'neef) oo<br /> Free: Language (High Realm)<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Dynast merits</i><br /> Resources ooo<br /> Followers o<br /> <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Language (Sea Tongue) o</span><br /> <br /> <u>Intimacies (definitely look over others)</u><br /> Defining Tie: House V'neef (Loyalty)<br /> Defining Principle: What is life without new experiences and challenges?<br /> Major Principle: I have contempt for those who abuse their power.<br /> Major Tie: My Sworn Brotherhood (Loyalty)<br /> Major Tie: Hundred Rivers and bird familiar (Best Friends)<br /> Major Tie: Uncle Sifu (Respect)<br /> Minor Principle: I adhere to the Immaculate Philosophy.<br /> Minor Tie: Myself (Pride)<br /> <br /> <u>Charms</u><br /> <i>Free Excellencies</i><br /> Brawl: Become the Hammer<br /> Archery: Unobstructed Hunter's Aim<br /> Dodge: Threshold Warding Stance<br /> Ride: Scatter Pearl Hoof Falls<br /> Integrity: Granite Curtain of Serenity<br /> <br /> Free: Daring Venture: Song of Sunlit Dreams<br /> 1. MA: Wood Dragon Vitality<br /> 2. MA: Eyes of the Wood Dragon<br /> 3. MA: Mind-Over-Body Meditation<br /> 4. MA: Soul-Marking Style<br /> 5. MA: Wood Dragon Form<br /> 6. Resistance: Ox-Body Technique<br /> 7. Resistance: Ox-Body Technique<br /> 8. <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Resistance: Ox-Body Technique</span><br /> 9. Survival: Beast-Taming Aspect<br /> 10. Survival: Mother-of-Beats Mastery<br /> 11. Ride: Heaven-Racing Leap<br /> 12. Daring Venture: Seeker's Heart Intuition<br /> 13. Performance: Swaying Boughs Arabesque<br /> 14. Performance: Petal Strewn Pavane<br /> 15. Daring Venture: Beckon the Wandering Wolf<br /> <br /> <u>Bonus Points</u><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">4 attributes</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">12 abilities</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">2 merits</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Going for:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Wood Dragon Style</span></span><br /> Survival: Ration-enhancing method, Quarry Revelation Technique, Beast-Taming Upgrade<br /> Performance: oratory and dance and a bunch others<br /> Ride<br /> White Reaper Style, or maybe the new Centipede Style in Lunars, which sounds poison-y which would fit the aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4620-tumbleweed664","user":"tumbleweed664","date":". 05-07-2020, 05:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4620-tumbleweed664","name":"tumbleweed664","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T01:03:45-07:00","id":1386308,"title":"","content":"I'd be curious if anyone does have anything to say about how effective Hundred Rivers is in combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T01:24:41-07:00","id":1386316,"title":"","content":"I need to sleep so I can\u2019t say much now, but you can still use Daring Venture. Any artifacts listed evocations are just one example of what they might give somebody, technically speaking everyone has, or can have, different evocations for the same artifact. The only thing is they should be somewhat close to the original themes of the artifact, and still stick within its material themes, so no flamethrower blue Jade lances or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T02:42:44-07:00","id":1386336,"title":"","content":"Yeah, on second thought I added Daring Venture back in, with the caveat that I may try/have to refluff it if House V'neef just doesn't work. I may switch those performance charms from dance and get vibrating strings defense if I plan to be mounted a fair bit. Given Daring Venture's backstory, seems easy enough to stunt by playing the bowstring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4620-tumbleweed664","user":"tumbleweed664","date":". 05-07-2020, 06:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4620-tumbleweed664","name":"tumbleweed664","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T13:05:27-07:00","id":1386466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tumbleweed664</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1384541-some-questions-on-db-charms-and-character-building?p=1386287#post1386287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [U]V'neef Avirat,</div> </div> </div> </div>He looks great. Hope you have a blast playing him.<br /> <br /> Some minor bean countery things from the top of my head, feel free to ignore, it's nothing that will make or break the character...<br /> <br /> 1. I'd maybe look at boosting dodge or shoring up your social stats a little, sacrificing athletics (for now) perhaps. You're only able to pump your evasion and resolve by 1 with your Excellencies as it stands, and you've got Petal Strewn Pavane to help with combat movement in any case. Maybe lean into that by leaving Athletics at 1 and boost it cheaply later as it's favoured?<br /> <br /> 2. You're very wilderness orientated but have a dot of mundane followers, what's your thinking, are they just typical Dynast servants, or something more? If you've got an idea then great, but I'd be tempted to ditch for something you can use all the time and isn't going to slow you down as you plunge into the wilderness.<br /> <br /> 3. Random question: Is it a game in the West as you're taking Seatongue? If you're going to be on a ship lots is a massive wolf going to be as useful as you'd like? Disregard if you're, say, going to be doing loads of guerilla type stuff on Caul or the like...<br /> <br /> Just random thoughts, far more important that he represents how you picture him. Have fun!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 05-07-2020, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T14:42:39-07:00","id":1386500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1384541-some-questions-on-db-charms-and-character-building?p=1386466#post1386466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He looks great. Hope you have a blast playing him.<br /> <br /> Some minor bean countery things from the top of my head, feel free to ignore, it's nothing that will make or break the character...<br /> <br /> 1. I'd maybe look at boosting dodge or shoring up your social stats a little, sacrificing athletics (for now) perhaps. You're only able to pump your evasion and resolve by 1 with your Excellencies as it stands, and you've got Petal Strewn Pavane to help with combat movement in any case. Maybe lean into that by leaving Athletics at 1 and boost it cheaply later as it's favoured?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, integrity and socialize are holes, I could move athletics there. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1384541-some-questions-on-db-charms-and-character-building?p=1386466#post1386466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. You're very wilderness orientated but have a dot of mundane followers, what's your thinking, are they just typical Dynast servants, or something more? If you've got an idea then great, but I'd be tempted to ditch for something you can use all the time and isn't going to slow you down as you plunge into the wilderness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Undeveloped mortal servants. I'd guess they are a little more ranger-y than the average dynastic servants (though I like the idea of the head servant being a more stuck up prig).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1384541-some-questions-on-db-charms-and-character-building?p=1386466#post1386466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Random question: Is it a game in the West as you're taking Seatongue? If you're going to be on a ship lots is a massive wolf going to be as useful as you'd like? Disregard if you're, say, going to be doing loads of guerilla type stuff on Caul or the like...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely flexible, I settled on Sea Tongue because of House V'neef's interests. Though as you note he is not a sailor-type so he might have learned something else<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1384541-some-questions-on-db-charms-and-character-building?p=1386466#post1386466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just random thoughts, far more important that he represents how you picture him. Have fun!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! I'm pretty excited about him!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4620-tumbleweed664","name":"tumbleweed664","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T15:09:21-07:00","id":1386508,"title":"","content":"Technically if you want to ride Hundred Rivers and use your artifact bow as a staff you can ride him into combat. Using your bow as a staff while mounted will give you a resting parry of 8, before charms, so...yeah pretty good. Otherwise hanging back at Short range while your deadly giant wolf goes in and pins them down is good,. using your bow for archery. Also note that he can be trained in any of the latent wolf abilities, like Loyal Guardian which lets him flurry a Defend Other action on you every round without penalties.<br /> <br /> Also his hardness makes him immune to your anima killing him unless he gets crashed.<br /> <br /> Double also dismounting is only a reflexive move action, I'm pretty sure, so if you wanted to swap to archery it's as easy as using your reflexive move to hop off and then start shooting.<br /> <br /> Plus even if you need to swap to a short bow to use archery from its back, there's other non-combat reasons to have a mount. Mostly any kind of test of speed where you're chasing down a fleeing cart full of cultists, or dashing away trying to outrace an avalanche or something. Or even just long distance travel to avoid fatigue, but I find that doesn't come up that often in most games.<br /> <br /> <br /> He does look very fun though! I agree with Moss that things you have just 3 dots in you might want to get a specialty in or another dot to up your cap, but it's not really that important depending on your ST. The dodge excellency already removes all environmental penalties to your Evasion and raises it by a point for 2m, if you want to raise it or grab a specialty in play it shouldn't kill you, especially since you'll be parrying most of the time anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 05-07-2020, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T18:20:37-07:00","id":1386850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1384541-some-questions-on-db-charms-and-character-building?p=1386508#post1386508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically if you want to ride Hundred Rivers and use your artifact bow as a staff you can ride him into combat. Using your bow as a staff while mounted will give you a resting parry of 8, before charms, so...yeah pretty good. Otherwise hanging back at Short range while your deadly giant wolf goes in and pins them down is good,. using your bow for archery. Also note that he can be trained in any of the latent wolf abilities, like Loyal Guardian which lets him flurry a Defend Other action on you every round without penalties.<br /> <br /> Also his hardness makes him immune to your anima killing him unless he gets crashed.<br /> <br /> Double also dismounting is only a reflexive move action, I'm pretty sure, so if you wanted to swap to archery it's as easy as using your reflexive move to hop off and then start shooting.<br /> <br /> Plus even if you need to swap to a short bow to use archery from its back, there's other non-combat reasons to have a mount. Mostly any kind of test of speed where you're chasing down a fleeing cart full of cultists, or dashing away trying to outrace an avalanche or something. Or even just long distance travel to avoid fatigue, but I find that doesn't come up that often in most games.<br /> <br /> <br /> He does look very fun though! I agree with Moss that things you have just 3 dots in you might want to get a specialty in or another dot to up your cap, but it's not really that important depending on your ST. The dodge excellency already removes all environmental penalties to your Evasion and raises it by a point for 2m, if you want to raise it or grab a specialty in play it shouldn't kill you, especially since you'll be parrying most of the time anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I hadn't considered that abilities that key defenses make sense to leave at even dots for excellency purposes, I'll move those around.<br /> <br /> I think Hundred Rivers gives me great flexibility, but should I be worried about him being too vulnerable? It's hard for me to estimate how tough and how deadly he is. On the other hand, I was looking at taking the Ride Wood signature but its boosts are tiny for Hundred Rivers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4620-tumbleweed664","name":"tumbleweed664","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T19:25:10-07:00","id":1386872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tumbleweed664</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1384541-some-questions-on-db-charms-and-character-building?p=1386850#post1386850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I hadn't considered that abilities that key defenses make sense to leave at even dots for excellency purposes, I'll move those around.<br /> <br /> I think Hundred Rivers gives me great flexibility, but should I be worried about him being too vulnerable? It's hard for me to estimate how tough and how deadly he is. On the other hand, I was looking at taking the Ride Wood signature but its boosts are tiny for Hundred Rivers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't really answer if he's tough/deadly enough. Like if your ST starts the first session with &quot;Roll Join Battle chudmonkeys, I have one of every second and third circle demon so far published and they're all coming for you&quot; then no, Hundred Rivers isn't enough and you should have spent your points loading up on exalted retainers and armies. On the other hand if you're investigating a divinely blessed group of pirate raiders who have enhanced mortal stats and the benefit of two semi-powerful gods on their side then Hundred Rivers will tear them to pieces.<br /> <br /> Also, don't count out Great Heart Companion just because you're applying it to an already beastly creature. He gets +1 hardness, which makes him immune to reset decisive attacks since he gets 3, if you pick Dex he gets a permanent +1 to all attacks, which considering he's already got 17 base damage and a grapple of 10 is pretty good. If you were applying these stat boosts to a horse, yeah it'd be proportionally bigger, but then you're just taking your non-combat horse mount and making it maybe worth rolling into combat? But not really with a max 7 die attack even with it?<br /> <br /> On Hundred Rivers you're taking a monstrous 3 dot familiar and making him even more deadly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T08:29:22-07:00","id":1386978,"title":"","content":"I'm jealous. I've been kinda wanting to play a character with Daring Venture for a while.<br /> <br /> The biggest problem with Hundred Rivers, in my opinion, is that he really shines when working with other hand-to-hand fighters (that Pack Hunting ability makes a huge difference in his ability to contribute to a fight with higher-end enemies directly), but he's attached to a <i>bow</i>. Still, when your team needs to dogpile a dangerous foe he should be a big help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T11:02:01-07:00","id":1387015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1384541-some-questions-on-db-charms-and-character-building?p=1386978#post1386978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm jealous. I've been kinda wanting to play a character with Daring Venture for a while.<br /> <br /> The biggest problem with Hundred Rivers, in my opinion, is that he really shines when working with other hand-to-hand fighters (that Pack Hunting ability makes a huge difference in his ability to contribute to a fight with higher-end enemies directly), but he's attached to a <i>bow</i>. Still, when your team needs to dogpile a dangerous foe he should be a big help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note in this case Daring Venture is being used with Wood Dragon, making it a melee weapon, so as long as at least two of your hearthmates use Close range weapons you get the full 3 autosuccesses on every attack. Actually considering that taking the strength option to boost its damage by 1 might not be a bad choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T15:43:11-07:00","id":1387100,"title":"","content":"Thanks, it sounds like Hundred Rivers can hold his own to a degree and that the ride wood sig is worth thinking more about. Also tempting to get the ride air sig and go full neverending story. I'm sad that one of the two familiar combat charms in survival is fire aura but you can't have it all. I also do think I may switch the dance charms to instrument charms if I'm going to be riding a mount a fair bit (the image of me strumming my sanxian laying on hundred rivers' back while we stroll through the forest is pretty great).<br /> <br /> Edit: Now my question is: how do I re-skin the Mouse of the Sun into a familiar for a DB?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4620-tumbleweed664","user":"tumbleweed664","date":". 05-09-2020, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4620-tumbleweed664","name":"tumbleweed664","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}